WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.130
Keanu Reeves film Replicas started off 2019
with a gigantic thud..

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:10.280
Poorly reviewed and little-seen, the bewildering
sci-fi drama has earned itself the distinction

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:13.640
of being the worst-performing wide release
of the actor's career.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:15.460
It's enough to make you say

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:16.280
"Whoa."

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:19.740
Make no mistake — Replicas is a bad movie.

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:25.440
With a 9% rating on Rotten Tomatoes across
33 reviews after opening weekend, it's

00:00:25.441 --> 00:00:31.109
enough to remind people of Johnny Mnemonic,
Keanu Reeves' sci-fi thriller flop from 1995.

00:00:31.109 --> 00:00:33.620
Is Replicas the worst thing Reeves has done?

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:34.360
It's pretty close.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:39.500
On top of terrible reviews from both critics
and audiences, the movie landed in thirteenth

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:45.809
place at the box office over its opening weekend
in January, making less than 2.4 million dollars

00:00:45.809 --> 00:00:48.260
from over 2,300 theaters.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:49.100
How bad is that?

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:53.780
Let's put it this way — the movie made less
money over that weekend than Bohemian Rhapsody

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:57.670
did — and that's after the Queen biopic
had already been in theaters for more than

00:00:57.670 --> 00:00:58.670
two months.

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:00.440
You've got to make an impression, darling."

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:05.020
While he doesn't always get credit for it,
Keanu Reeves has always been a versatile leading

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:05.520
man.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:10.480
He can anchor action movies and sappy romances,
and thanks to the success of The Matrix, he

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:13.500
also has street cred when it comes to sci-fi
and fantasy.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:17.979
Unfortunately, he seems to have been sorely
miscast as the lead of Replicas, playing a

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:22.420
grief-stricken mad scientist who clones his
family after a fatal car accident.

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:26.640
He turns in a good performance, but it's not
enough to carry the movie, much less sell

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:27.280
the character.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:31.280
Several reviewers have indicated that the
role would be better suited for an actor like

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:35.660
Nicolas Cage, who could take the crazy concept
and run with it in a way that Reeves can't

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:36.160
match.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:37.880
"I NEVER MISFILED ANYTHING!

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:40.540
NOT ONCE — NOT ONE TIME!!!!"

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:46.020
Replicas was distributed by Entertainment
Studios, a company which focuses on smaller

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:49.860
releases like Hostiles, Chappaquiddick, and
47 Meters Down.

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:53.940
They're the sort of movies that you would
expect to go direct to DVD or streaming — and

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:57.160
in the case of Replicas, that's probably what
should have happened.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:03.200
According to Deadline, Entertainment Studios
sank at least $10.5 million into TV ads for

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:07.000
Replicas, which in retrospect appears to have
been a major waste of money.

00:02:07.009 --> 00:02:11.380
Instead of releasing the movie onto digital
services to quietly fend for itself, the company

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:15.970
tried to sell it as a theater-worthy experience
with a wide release, seemingly only upping

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:17.020
their financial risk.

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:21.400
After such a terrible opening weekend, it's
hard to see how the movie can ever make its

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:22.080
money back.

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:25.240
"What if something horrible goes wrong?"

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:27.880
"Something already has."

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:33.060
While Replicas has its fair share of unique
problems, the movie also suffers from a trend

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:36.200
that almost always plagues theaters during
the first weeks of a year.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:41.120
While there are occasionally successful exceptions,
people generally don't see that many movies

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:45.120
in January, giving it a reputation as the
worst month at the box office.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:50.200
Movies released in December gross an average
of over $1.5 billion combined.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:56.320
But January's average box office is drastically
smaller, coming in at around only $405 million.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:59.840
It's a trend that's been around for a long
time — people don't want to go out to see

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:04.080
movies after an exhausting holiday, especially
when the weather tends to be bad.

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:08.280
When people do go out to the movies, they
typically go to play catch-up, seeing the

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:11.180
movies they missed out on before they leave
theaters for good.

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:16.360
Since audience turnout is so much lower in
January, studios tend to use the month to

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:20.640
release their worst movies, making as much
money as they can while the competition is

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:21.140
light.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:26.260
Audiences have clued in to this phenomenon,
and as a result, many viewers know to be suspicious

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:27.760
of January releases.

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:32.300
When a movie gets plum placement during the
spring, summer, or holiday season, it's usually

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:35.120
a sign of a studio's confidence in the movie's
quality.

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:40.420
When it comes out in the dead month of January,
like Replicas did, it tends to suggest exactly

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:41.060
the opposite.

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:46.220
Replicas started filming in August 2016, but
didn't show up in theaters until the second

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:47.800
weekend of 2019.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:50.600
After years in the making, it landed with
a thud.

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:51.500
What happened?

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:55.860
There are many reasons why a movie can end
up with a big delay between shooting and release.

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:58.580
But a long gap is rarely an encouraging sign.

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:03.060
It can suggest a movie that's proving difficult
to assemble in the edit, or be a sign of a

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:07.590
movie that's just so bad that producers have
trouble finding a distributor, which previously

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:11.700
seemed to be the case with 2018 flops Gotti
and Holmes and Watson.

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:16.290
A long delay doesn't guarantee a bad movie,
but combined with a January release date,

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:20.720
it raises real warning signs — signs that
in Replicas' case turned out to be totally

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:21.540
on point.

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:26.440
As big of a failure as Replicas turned out
to be, the expectations for the movie were

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:27.300
never that high.

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:32.780
While it's definitely a blemish on Keanu Reeves'
filmography, it's not exactly a career killer.

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:36.850
The only people who seem likely to suffer
from Replicas bombing are the people behind

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:41.650
the cameras, who were responsible for the
movie's incomprehensible script, flat direction,

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:42.980
and confusing edit.

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:44.480
Those people might be in trouble.

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:48.700
But the actors in the movie did pretty decent
work, considering what they had to work with.

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:53.640
It's been so long since the movie was filmed,
it's possible the cast has forgotten Replicas

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:58.100
even exists — and by the time 2019 is over,
so will everybody else.

